  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{np}=4, \\mathrm{npq}=2$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{q}=\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{p}=\\frac{1}{2} \\therefore \\mathrm{n}=8$\r\n$\\mathrm{p}(\\mathrm{x}=2)={ }^{8} \\mathrm{C}_{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{8}=\\frac{28}{256}=\\frac{7}{64}$",
